A1. What does a lawyer do when he refers to a similar case? ~ CITES
A6. What are good places for mud-slingers? ~ SLEWS
A11. What word did the President send to the people? ~ CHOOSE
A12. Where do the beautiful eyes beckon? ~ HITHER
A14. Who are always shooting around the Orient? ~ CHINESE
A15. What makes the stars come out? ~ ENCORES
A17. Name that fabulous bird of Arabia. ~ ROC
A18. What did William Tell do to make his mark? ~ AIMED
A20. What puts the holes in the cheese? ~ RAT
A21. What is the blue and yellow macaw of Brazil? ~ ARA
A22. What makes a good definition? ~ SYNONYM
A24. What girl often helps in constructing Crossword Puzzles? ~ ADA
A25. Who do the pious think will have a hot time bye and bye? ~ PAGAN
A27. What would be a good name for a funny looking guy? ~ GUY
A28. What part of anything is never on the inside? ~ OUTER
A30. What is a good advertising salesman? ~ SLOGAN
A32. What would be good in a pinch? (Plural) ~ BALERS
A33. What does too much of your salary go for? ~ APARTMENT
A34. What do people use when they can't work a typewriter? ~ SCRIPT
A37. What kind of a man was the Kaiser? ~ GERMAN
A41. Where did her ring come from? ~ PHONE
A42. What does many a bad actor try to do? ~ ACT
A44. What does the elevator operator give the white collar-man? ~ RAISE
A45. What do chorus girls like to do? ~ EAT
A46. Who gives orders to the Duke? ~ DUCHESS
A49. What is a definite article? ~ THE
A50. Where is the steerage? (Dumb Dora knows you can't steer from the bow.) ~ AFT
A51. What sweet thing hangs around the perfume counter? ~ SCENT
A52. What is short for a drink? ~ TOD
A53. What do publishers do after a sell-out? ~ REISSUE
A56. What are sponges? ~ SOAKERS
A59. What are indications of contempt? ~ SNEERS
A60. What has a lot of pull? ~ ENGINE
A61. What fought the Blues in 1861? ~ GRAYS
A62. What keeps coming up after being put down? ~ SEEDS

D1. Where should the news, that the Revolutionary War is all over, be sent? ~ CHICAGO
D2. What is an electrified particle? ~ ION
D3. Where is the first hole usually located? ~ TOE
D4. What composition is difficult for many scientists? ~ ESSAY
D5. What are sightseers always doing? ~ SEEING
D6. How do the old pair of trousers look? ~ SHEENY
D7. Name a very popular American. ~ LINDY
D8. What much used abbreviation means "and there are others?" ~ ETC
D9. What pronoun indicates lots of curiosity? ~ WHO
D10. What adjective describes the notched edge of a leaf? ~ SERRATE
D11. What kind of music comes from a chorus? ~ CHORAL
D13. Who read Shakespeare at the age of ten? ~ READER
D14. What are they always shooting down South? ~ CRAPS
D16. What are the brightest tbings in Hollywood? ~ STARS
D19. What is a growing ambition with some young men? ~ MOUSTACHE
D22. How did she answer when angry? (Past tense.) ~ SNAPPED
D23. What people are often seen in dental offices? ~ MOANERS
D26. What adverb means "once more?" ~ AGAIN
D29. What is an extremist? ~ ULTRA
D31. Give a little nickname. ~ NAT
D32. What do some leisure people do for a living? ~ BEG
D34. What was a pointed argument effectively used in the middle ages? ~ SPEAR
D35. What word means "irritate?" ~ CHAFES
D36. What is many a bad egg doing at the present time? ~ ROTTING
D38. What has thumbs but no fingers? ~ MITTENS
D39. What do the swells of the ocean wash? ~ ASHORE
D40. What does any family have an abundance of? ~ NEEDS
D42. What is a good approach? ~ ACCESS
D43. What is the past, present, and future of verbs? (Plural.) ~ TENSES
D47. What is "taking too much interest?" ~ USURY
D48. What age was not so soft for the women folks? ~ STONE
D54. What is an abbreviation for something sleep-producing? (Procurable Sunday Mornings) ~ SER
D55. What is deep stuff? ~ SEA
D57. What is it women like to keep to themselves? ~ AGE
D58. What could you call a very little butter? ~ KID


Misprints, kept as printed (printed → meant):
D16: What are the brightest tbings in Hollywood? → things

